              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Marathi for to grow rough, then the Marathi for to slosh about."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: किनारपट्टी",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "किनारपट्टी — kinārpaṭṭī — \"a coastline\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "इथली किनारपट्टी खूप सुंदर आहे. ithlī kinārpaṭṭī khūp sundar āhe. The coastline here is very beautiful."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Feminine."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Built on किनारा, a shore, and पट्टी, a strip: a long strip of shore."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "किनारपट्टी (kinārpaṭṭī) is a Marathi compound of किनारा, \"a shore\", a loan usually traced to Persian kinār, and पट्टी, \"a strip\"."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
